ndset, and empathy for users.",body:"My career path into IT is built on continuous self-study, certifications, and hands-on support experience. Before IT, I ran a small restaurant, worked as a chef, sold B2B products overseas, taught adults English one-on-one, and coached people in fitness. That background helps me stay calm under pressure and explain technical steps clearly to non-technical users.",points:["Good at explaining technical issues to non-technical users without making them feel judged.","I was already writing KB articles, training notes, and process guides before AI tools became common. Today I use AI carefully to draft and organize faster while respecting data-security boundaries.","Still actively learning Linux, programming with AI coding tools, cybersecurity, AI agents, and additional language basics including Japanese, Spanish, and French."]},skills:{title:"Skills",heading:"Solid technical support foundations, strong documentation habits, and cross-cultural communication skills.",groups:[{name:"ITSM & Support",items:["ServiceNow incident and request handling","ITIL 4 Foundation","SLA awareness","L1.5 troubleshooting","Clear escalation notes"]},{name:"Endpoint & Microsoft 365",items:["Windows 10/11","Outlook / Teams / OneDrive","Microsoft 365 Admin basics","Active Directory","VPN and MFA support"]},{name:"Knowledge & Training",items:["KB articles","Onboarding material","Process walkthroughs","Training videos and notes","One-on-one coaching"]},{name:"AI Tools & Automation",items:["Microsoft Copilot","ChatGPT / Gemini / DeepSeek","Codex CLI and AI agents","Prompt and system prompt design","Power Automate basics"]},{name:"Communication & Learning",items:["Fluent working English","Native Mandarin","Cross-cultural support","Dedao learner, 963 credits","Technology and AI news tracking"]}]},experience:{title:"Work Experience",heading:"A path from customer work to global IT support.",roles:[{period:"Apr 2022 - Present",company:"Kyndryl (IBM infrastructure services heritage)",role:"IT Technical Support Specialist, L1.5 / ServiceNow",location:"Shenzhen / Remote",bullets:["Converted to full-time Kyndryl employee in Apr 2022, about nine months after joining the IBM/Kyndryl support environment through ASDC, with consistent ticket resolution quality and user communication.","Support Yageo global manufacturing IT users through English phone, email, chat, and remote troubleshooting across Windows, Microsoft 365, VPN, MFA, account, endpoint, and application issues.","Also supported the AIA service desk project for about one year; helped rebuild detailed knowledge documents, training material, and video-style walkthroughs for a long-running project that needed clearer handover material.","Keep improving the Yageo knowledge base from real incidents. The habit started as manual documentation work before AI tools were common; today I use AI carefully to draft, organize, and review support notes without exposing sensitive data."]},{period:"Jul 2021 - Apr 2022",company:"ASDC / IBM-Kyndryl UPS Project",role:"Bilingual Technical Support Representative",location:"Shenzhen",bullets:["Provided English and Mandarin support for UPS internal users and external customers in a 24/7 support environment.","Handled software, hardware, account access, and office productivity issues within SLA expectations, then escalated complex cases with clear diagnostic notes.","Built the call discipline, patience, and written handoff style that later helped me move into full-time Kyndryl support."]},{period:"Jul 2019 - Jul 2021",company:"Shenzhen A-Smart Technology & Development",role:"B2B Foreign Trade Sales Representative / English Livestreamer",location:"Shenzhen",bullets:["Managed Alibaba international B2B sales for automotive electronics products and communicated with overseas customers in English.","Used product demos, livestreaming, written follow-up, and repeat-process notes to make customer communication more consistent.","This role pushed my English 